val xs = List(1, 2, 3, 4, 5)
xs.view.map(<some function> -- In this line nothing gets computed a view just stores the recipe, not the results
    once we perform some action that's when it triggers the computation until the action is satisfied
    The downside the chain gets recomputed on every traversal

xs.to(LazyList).map(<some function>) -- LazyList is exactly same as view but the results are cached instead of
    recomputing if we perform the same computation the value that is cached is returned if your action is
    different then all the elements required to compute that action are stored
    The downside for very large actions this can cause memory issues as the elements gets cached in memory

If the function you pass returns an Option too, use flatMap, not map. map nests, flatMap flattens

